WEBVTT

00:00:10.006 --> 00:00:21.349
Ski Race by Eleanor Jop It's Sunday.

00:00:21.409 --> 00:00:27.670
Sue, Rebecca and their friends arrive at their holiday chalet.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.891
Everybody is very excited.

00:00:30.951 --> 00:00:33.552
They are going to ski.

00:00:33.612 --> 00:00:36.702
Sue and Rebecca love skiing.

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:39.555
They are good at skiing.

00:00:39.615 --> 00:00:43.270
It's early on Monday morning.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:47.553
Everybody is at the ski higher shop.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:52.848
Sue and Rebecca are choosing their boots and skis.

00:00:52.908 --> 00:00:57.992
They put on their boots and carry their skis.

00:00:58.052 --> 00:01:03.587
Sue has yellow boots and blue skis.

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:09.127
Rebecca has red boots and white skis.

00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:13.864
Sue's poles are sticking out behind her.

00:01:13.924 --> 00:01:18.895
Mark trips over Sue's skis.

00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:22.016
Are you okay?

00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:25.856
Your friend's ski poles are in the way.

00:01:25.916 --> 00:01:30.088
You've got big feet.

00:01:30.148 --> 00:01:33.898
The snow looks hard.

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:38.141
Yes, the skiing will be fast today.

00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:42.326
Sue and Rebecca are in the ski lift.

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:46.298
The hard snow of the beast is below them.

00:01:46.358 --> 00:01:51.392
The ski lift is taking them to the top of the mountain.

00:01:51.452 --> 00:01:59.087
They are going to ski down the beast from the top of the mountain.

00:01:59.147 --> 00:02:07.356
Sue and Rebecca get off the ski lift at the top of the mountain.

00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:10.812
Then they ski down the mountain.

00:02:10.872 --> 00:02:13.373
They are good skiers.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.984
They don't fall over.

00:02:16.044 --> 00:02:19.396
David and Mark are watching them.

00:02:19.456 --> 00:02:24.750
David and Mark are also good skiers.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:32.664
They're good skiers, but we're better.

00:02:32.724 --> 00:02:37.648
The young people ski all day.

00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:40.622
They enjoy themselves.

00:02:40.682 --> 00:02:45.345
In the evening, they ski back to their shallow.

00:02:45.405 --> 00:02:51.479
They are very tired.

00:02:51.539 --> 00:02:57.564
It's Wednesday morning.

00:02:57.624 --> 00:03:02.096
The young people are waiting to go up on the ski lift.

00:03:02.156 --> 00:03:05.246
They are listening to their teacher.

00:03:05.306 --> 00:03:08.754
There's going to be a ski race.

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:12.067
Sue and Rebecca want to win.

00:03:12.126 --> 00:03:15.318
David and Mark want to win.

00:03:15.378 --> 00:03:18.781
Everybody wants to win.

00:03:18.841 --> 00:03:22.794
We're arranging a race on Saturday.

00:03:22.854 --> 00:03:25.816
That's the last day of the holiday.

00:03:25.876 --> 00:03:29.418
The race is 10 kilometres long.

00:03:29.478 --> 00:03:32.530
It's a long and difficult piece.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:38.940
Who wants to race?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:46.472
The young people go up the mountain.

00:03:46.532 --> 00:03:49.074
They put on their skis.

00:03:49.134 --> 00:03:52.076
They ski down the pist.

00:03:52.136 --> 00:03:55.509
They are practising for the race.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:59.733
Sue and Rebecca are skiing fast.

00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:02.865
They want to win the race.

00:04:02.925 --> 00:04:07.576
Mark and David are also skiing fast.

00:04:07.636 --> 00:04:13.508
They want to pass Sue and Rebecca, but they can't.

00:04:13.568 --> 00:04:19.670
Look at them, they want to win, but we're going to win.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:26.442
It's difficult, yes, but it's fun.

00:04:26.502 --> 00:04:31.153
It's Saturday morning.

00:04:31.212 --> 00:04:35.424
Saturday is the last day of the holiday.

00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:38.324
It's the day of the race.

00:04:38.384 --> 00:04:42.096
The race is in the afternoon.

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:45.598
Sue and Rebecca are hungry.

00:04:45.657 --> 00:04:49.729
They leave their skis at the side of the cafe.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:55.802
They sit down and order lunch.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:05:00.048
I'm hungry.

00:05:00.108 --> 00:05:02.704
A large hamburger please.

00:05:02.763 --> 00:05:08.236
A large pizza and a large coke please.

00:05:08.296 --> 00:05:13.660
David and Mark see Sue and Rebecca.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.402
They don't want Sue and Rebecca to win the race.

00:05:18.462 --> 00:05:22.975
They find Rebecca and Sue's skis.

00:05:23.034 --> 00:05:28.446
They undo a screw on one of Sue's skis.

00:05:28.506 --> 00:05:32.066
These are Sue's blue skis.

00:05:32.126 --> 00:05:34.377
I'll undo the binding.

00:05:34.437 --> 00:05:35.567
Good.

00:05:35.627 --> 00:05:38.838
Now the skis won't work.

00:05:38.898 --> 00:05:44.698
We're sure to win.

00:05:44.758 --> 00:05:50.720
Everybody is ready.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.210
The race is starting.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.880
Who is going to win?

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.708
Our Sue and Rebecca are going to win.

00:05:58.768 --> 00:06:02.714
Are David and Mark going to win?

00:06:02.774 --> 00:06:06.275
Come on Sue and Rebecca!

00:06:06.335 --> 00:06:09.096
Come on David and Mark!

00:06:09.156 --> 00:06:15.607
On your marks, get set, go!

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:21.068
Sue and Rebecca are in front.

00:06:21.128 --> 00:06:24.839
Then Sue's ski comes off.

00:06:24.899 --> 00:06:26.626
Sue falls.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:33.304
She slides across the snow and off the piece.

00:06:33.364 --> 00:06:38.564
Rebecca stops to help her.

00:06:38.624 --> 00:06:42.445
David and Mark ski past.

00:06:42.505 --> 00:06:45.246
Mark shouts to David.

00:06:45.306 --> 00:06:46.786
Ha ha!

00:06:46.846 --> 00:06:50.276
The screw on her binding is undone.

00:06:50.336 --> 00:06:53.802
We're going to win!

00:06:53.862 --> 00:06:58.872
Sue and Rebecca repair Sue's ski.

00:06:58.932 --> 00:07:01.916
Now Sue can ski again.

00:07:01.976 --> 00:07:04.368
They look for the beast.

00:07:04.428 --> 00:07:07.682
Suddenly they see the beast.

00:07:07.742 --> 00:07:11.726
They see the other skiers.

00:07:11.786 --> 00:07:22.447
Now they are racing again.

00:07:22.507 --> 00:07:32.316
Sue and Rebecca come first.

00:07:32.376 --> 00:07:34.858
They win the race.

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.810
It's the end of the holiday.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.331
Back home tomorrow.

00:07:40.391 --> 00:07:44.304
Congratulations Sue and Rebecca.

00:07:44.364 --> 00:07:46.605
It's not fair.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:49.237
We are first.

00:07:49.296 --> 00:07:52.468
We are the winners.

00:07:52.528 --> 00:07:54.740
Well done.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.561
Well done.

00:07:56.621 --> 00:07:57.542
Brilliant.
